The driver provides support for the MCP980x series of temperature
sensors.   It  allows  reporting  ambient temperature through the
API.  The following variable are provided: ADC resolution  (inte‐
ger).   Valid  values  are 0‐3, where 0 is 9‐bit (0.5 Celsius de‐
gree) and 3 is 12‐bit (0.0625 Celsius degree) resolution.  If the
ambient temperature exceeds this limit, the chip asserts an alert
line (integer).  Hysteresis for temperature limit (integer).  The
device first appeared in The driver was written  by  MCP9804  and
MCP9805  chip are different and are supported by the driver.  The
MCP980x chip supports hysteresis  and  temperature  limit  values
with  a resolution of 0.5 Celsius degree, however the driver sup‐
ports setting only integer values.
